/* book exam traps: Do not swap the stick shaker and stick pusher. The shaker warns; the pusher acts. | The gear warning needs gear not down plus throttles at idle, or landing flap; gear up at high power does not sound it. | A squat switch is not a lock switch. It senses weight on the strut; lock and door positions come from proximity sensors. | Asymmetry compares left with right wing; skew compares panels on the same wing. Both stop the drive. | Stall speed varies as √W, so a heavier aircraft stalls faster: 20 % more weight gives √1.2 = 1.095, about 9.5 % more speed. */
